<title>JAPAN: Tokyo Nov dept store sales down 0.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Tokyo Nov dept store sales down 0.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales at Tokyo department stores declined 0.3 percent in November from a year earlier to 217.0 billion yen, the Japan Department Stores' Association said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The November figure showed the first year-on-year fall since July, the association said in a statement.</p>
<p>The survey covers 30 outlets of 14 department store operators.</p>
<p>Sales to individual customers were brisk in November but sales to corporate clients declined, the association said.</p>
<p>Despite the fall in November, department store sales are still gradually recovering, the association said.</p>
</text>
